WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Cut an A4 sheet of paper exactly in half.

2
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.210
Lay one half on the full
sheet, corner to corner.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.940
The diagonals line up:
same shape, smaller.

4
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.760
A4 is two hundred and ten by two
hundred and ninety-seven millimetres.

5
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:20.150
Long side over short side is very
nearly the square root of two.

6
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.980
Is that just a handy choice?

7
00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.660
Or must the ratio be root two?

8
00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:29.720
In this mission, you'll work with
surds: exact roots like root two.

9
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.650
You'll see why root two times
root two is exactly two,

10
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.280
and how to rationalise a fraction.

11
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:41.430
Your mission: explain why a sheet that
keeps its shape when halved must have sides

12
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.150
in the ratio root two.
